  "text8": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "style": {
     "from": "leadWide"
    },
    "text": "Two years ago every service of ours talked to the others through its own private channel. Last spring we replaced all of them with a single queue. This is what went well, and what we would do differently."
   }
  },
  "text9": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "style": {
     "from": "heading2Wide"
    },
    "text": "Why one queue"
   }
  },
  "text10": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "text": "Forty services meant forty ways to retry, forty dead-letter conventions and forty dashboards nobody fully trusted. When an incident crossed three services, we spent the first hour just working out where a message had been lost.",
    "style": {
     "from": "bodyWide"
    }
   }
  },
  "text11": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "text": "A shared queue gave us one place to look. Ordering, retries and visibility became properties of the platform instead of habits of each team.",
    "style": {
     "from": "bodyWide"
    }
   }
  },
  "column12": {
   "type": "column",
   "layout": {
    "padding": [
     20,
     4,
     0,
     4
    ],
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "crossAxisAlignment": "start"
   },
   "decoration": {
    "strokes": [
     {
      "color": "primary"
     }
    ],
    "strokeSides": "left"
   },
   "children": [
    "text12"
   ]
  },
  "text12": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "text": "The queue did not make our systems simpler. It made their complexity visible, and that was worth more.",
    "style": {
     "from": "bodyWide",
     "fontSize": 22,
     "fontWeight": 600,
     "color": "#FF1F2A44"
    }
   }
  },
  "text13": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "style": {
     "from": "heading2Wide"
    },
    "text": "What the migration taught us"
   }
  },
  "text14": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "text": "We moved services in waves of five, starting with the ones that could fail without anyone noticing. Each wave used the same small producer wrapper, so every message carried an id, a schema version and a retry budget.",
    "style": {
     "from": "bodyWide"
    }
   }
  },
  "CodeBlock1": {
   "type": "CodeBlock",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "title": "producer.ts",
    "code": "const msg = {\n  id: uuid(),\n  schema: 'orders.v2',\n  retries: 5,\n  body: payload,\n};\nawait queue.publish('orders', msg);",
    "language": "typescript",
    "copyable": true
   }
  },
  "text15": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "text": "The wrapper looks trivial, and that is the point: the less each team had to decide, the faster the waves went.",
    "style": {
     "from": "bodyWide"
    }
   }
  },
  "text16": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "style": {
     "from": "strongWide"
    },
    "text": "Three things we would do again:"
   }
  },
